GUI:TextureFilter
"Texture Filtering"
END

GUI:TextureFilter0
"Bilinear"
END

GUI:TextureFilter1
"Trilinear"
END

GUI:TextureFilter2
"Anisotropic"
END

TOOLTIP:TextureFilter
"How textures are sampled as they recede from the camera. Bilinear is what the game shipped with and makes distant ground shimmer; anisotropic keeps it sharp. Takes effect the next time the display device is reset."
END

GUI:Anisotropy
"Anisotropic Samples"
END

TOOLTIP:Anisotropy
"How many samples anisotropic filtering may take. Auto lets the graphics card decide, up to 16. Only used when texture filtering is anisotropic."
END

GUI:AnisotropyCardMaximum
"Auto"
END

GUI:TextureResolution
"Texture Resolution"
END

GUI:ParticleLimit
"Particle Limit"
END

GUI:NeverLowerDetail
"Never Lower Detail"
END

