// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// One GUI: label and one TOOLTIP: line per row of TheOptionCatalog.  A label
// and the combo box under it share the tooltip; an OPTION_ENUM row also needs
// its entries, numbered from zero in the order the enum declares them.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

GUI:WindowMode
"Window Mode"
END

GUI:WindowMode0
"Fullscreen"
END

GUI:WindowMode1
"Borderless"
END

GUI:WindowMode2
"Windowed"
END

TOOLTIP:WindowMode
"Fullscreen takes the display mode, borderless covers it with a window and alt-tabs instantly. Borderless picks the resolution itself, so the list on the left is yours in the other two."
END

GUI:MSAA
"Antialiasing"
END

GUI:MSAA0
"Off"
END

GUI:MSAA1
"2x"
END

GUI:MSAA2
"4x"
END

GUI:MSAA3
"8x"
END

GUI:MSAA4
"16x"
END

TOOLTIP:MSAA
"Smooths the stair steps along model edges. A level your card does not offer drops to the highest one it does. Applied when the display device is next reset."
END

GUI:Bloom
"Glow"
END

GUI:Bloom0
"Off"
END

GUI:Bloom1
"Subtle"
END

GUI:Bloom2
"Normal"
END

GUI:Bloom3
"Strong"
END

TOOLTIP:Bloom
"How far bright surfaces bleed light into what is around them. Retail had none of this, so Off is what the artwork was painted for."
END

GUI:BloomThreshold
"What Glows"
END

GUI:BloomThreshold0
"Only the brightest"
END

GUI:BloomThreshold1
"Bright things"
END

GUI:BloomThreshold2
"Most of the picture"
END

TOOLTIP:BloomThreshold
"How much of the screen is bright enough to glow at all. Only the brightest keeps it to muzzle flashes and lamps; most of the picture puts a haze over the whole battlefield."
END

GUI:VSync
"Vertical Sync"
END

TOOLTIP:VSync
"Holds the picture to the monitor so it does not tear. Off, the picture runs as fast as the machine draws. Applied when you Accept."
END

GUI:MiddleMousePans
"Middle Mouse Pans"
END

TOOLTIP:MiddleMousePans
"Hold the middle button to drag the map under the cursor."
END

GUI:ZoomToCursor
"Zoom To Cursor"
END

TOOLTIP:ZoomToCursor
"The wheel zooms towards whatever the cursor is over instead of the middle of the screen."
END

GUI:EdgeScrollWindowed
"Edge Scroll In A Window"
END

TOOLTIP:EdgeScrollWindowed
"Retail refuses to scroll from the screen edge in windowed mode. Turn this on to get it back on a second monitor or in borderless."
END

GUI:SnapCamera45
"Snap Camera Rotation"
END

TOOLTIP:SnapCamera45
"Rotating the camera clicks to the eight 45 degree headings instead of stopping anywhere."
END

GUI:GridBuild
"Grid Building Placement"
END

TOOLTIP:GridBuild
"Structures land on the pathfinder's own 10-unit grid, so two buildings put down by eye share an edge instead of leaving a gap too narrow to walk through."
END

GUI:NudgeBuild
"Nudge Blocked Placement"
END

TOOLTIP:NudgeBuild
"A structure whose spot is blocked slides to the nearest one it fits instead of going red under the cursor."
END

GUI:SnapBuild45
"Snap Building Rotation"
END

TOOLTIP:SnapBuild45
"Drag-to-rotate clicks to the eight 45 degree headings, which is what walls and defenses along a base edge want."
END

GUI:RangeRing
"Placement Range Ring"
END

TOOLTIP:RangeRing
"Draws the weapon range of the structure you are about to place."
END

GUI:WorkersReturn
"Workers Return To Supply"
END

TOOLTIP:WorkersReturn
"A worker that finishes a building goes back to gathering instead of standing where it built."
END

GUI:BuildTooltips
"Detailed Build Tooltips"
END

TOOLTIP:BuildTooltips
"Build buttons list cost, build time and prerequisites."
END

GUI:HudOverlay
"HUD Overlay"
END

TOOLTIP:HudOverlay
"The extra readouts across the top of the screen: power, income and the production strip."
END

GUI:ArchiveReplays
"Archive Replays"
END

TOOLTIP:ArchiveReplays
"Every game is kept under its own name instead of overwriting the last one."
END

GUI:HealthBars
"Health Bars"
END

GUI:HealthBars0
"Always"
END

GUI:HealthBars1
"Smart"
END

GUI:HealthBars2
"Selection Only"
END

GUI:HealthBars3
"Never"
END

TOOLTIP:HealthBars
"Smart shows a bar over anything hurt, plus the selection and whatever is under the cursor. Selection only is what retail did."
END

GUI:PlayerColors
"Player Colors"
END

GUI:PlayerColors0
"Original"
END

GUI:PlayerColors1
"You, Allies, Enemies"
END

GUI:PlayerColors2
"By Team"
END

TOOLTIP:PlayerColors
"You, allies, enemies paints you blue, everyone on your side green and everyone shooting at you red. By team gives each alliance its own color and each member of it a shade. Your own screen only, so it changes nothing for anyone else in the game."
END

// Peace time - the lobby combo box, its tooltip, the corner countdown and the three things the game
// says while the clock runs.  Tools/peacetime_layout.py selfcheck fails if any of these goes missing.

GUI:PeaceTimeOff
"No Peace Time"
END

GUI:PeaceTimeFormat
"Peace: %d min"
END

TOOLTIP:PeaceTime
"Nobody can attack for this long at the start of the match. Anything that walks up to an enemy command center burns."
END

GUI:PeaceTimeStarted
"Peace time: %d minutes. Nobody can attack until it runs out."
END

GUI:PeaceTimeRemaining
"Peace time ends in %d seconds."
END

GUI:PeaceTimeOver
"Peace time is over."
END

GUI:PeaceTimeHud
"%d:%02d"
END

GUI:PeaceTimeHudLabel
"PEACE"
END

GUI:LobbyTabChat
"Chat"
END

GUI:LobbyTabInfo
"Info"
END

GUI:LobbyTabSettings
"Lobby Settings"
END

GUI:PeaceTimeLabel
"Peace Time"
END

GUI:Superweapons
"Superweapons"
END

GUI:SuperweaponsAllow
"Allow Superweapons"
END

GUI:SuperweaponsLimit
"Limit Superweapons"
END

GUI:SuperweaponsNone
"No Superweapons"
END

TOOLTIP:Superweapons
"How many of each superweapon a player may have standing. Allow: as many as he can pay for. Limit: one each, and four for the USA Superweapon General. No: none at all, except the Superweapon General, who keeps one. He is the exception because his three superweapons are what he pays for a weaker army with."
END

GUI:UnitLimit
"Unit Limit"
END

TOOLTIP:UnitLimit
"840 units shared out evenly between the players: two players get 420 each, eight get 105. Units standing and units waiting in a queue both count, buildings do not. Your own count and your share are in the top right corner during the match."
END
